plugin-hostd (0.20.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: a manual staged run hands this layer's packages to the next
    without the channel
  * image-build: take the Open-Mixer Zynthian forks, branch openmixer
  * fuzz: key every mutant/input record from one place, src/fuzz_records.h
  * doc: document the fuzz record indirection through src/fuzz_records.h
  * release: 0.20.3
  * describe: a CLAP control's meaning from its declared panel's role,
    through the contract directory's role tables
  * formats: a declared panel's role is the one panel field that is a word
  * describe: CLAP meters become meters[], a parameter's contract its symbol,
    unit, scale and step
  * formats: the LV2 table reads urn:openmixer:unit#ratio as ratio
  * transforms: output-symbol, a CLAP meter's name made the symbol a host
    reads it by
  * describe: the omx-comp test holds CLAP meters to the descriptor's meters[]
  * main: --search-path, the LV2 and CLAP lists the daemon searches and their
    sources
  * docs: plugin-hostd --search-path prints the directories the daemon
    searches
  * pins: first use learns a binary linked out of a bundle in the search path
  * docs: first use judges a plugin's path as listed and hashes the file it
    resolves to
  * describe: the omx-comp fixture is omx-clap-scan's own dump
  * tests: fake-host writes a standard LV2 pset bundle on preset_save
  * supervisor: preset_show <uri> is answered by the LV2 world, not mod-host
    alone
  * bench: teardown removes its /tmp/omx-bench-* work dir also when --logs
    keeps the logs elsewhere
  * formats: a CLAP worker's CLAP_PATH carries its own preset search
  * docs/presets: LV2 user presets are pset bundles, our format is CLAP only
  * lv2: a manifest's leading UTF-8 BOM no longer swallows its first @prefix
    (#4)
  * describe: a red test holds a CLAP omx-comp's meters and units to its LV2
    twin
  * ci: packaging runs on v* tags and workflow_dispatch only
  * bench: an unreadable capture fails its row, not the pass

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:18:02 +0000
